Camera: the phone's cameras become the device's

The A4's camera ISP has always been modelled well enough for the guest to
drive it -- it draws a test pattern, on time, into the buffer the kext gave it,
and both cameras' drivers accept it. What it never had was a picture. This is
that, written as the smallest thing that can be: a hand-off between the app's
camera thread and the emulated ISP.

  hw/arm/host-camera.c            two slots, one per sensor. A push copies the
                                  frame and, if nobody drew the last one, counts
                                  it as replaced -- a viewfinder drops, it does
                                  not queue, so a slow guest costs a dropped
                                  frame and never a growing buffer. A take hands
                                  the newest frame over once. Sizes that cannot
                                  be a picture are refused rather than drawn.
  hw/arm/s5l8930_isp.c            the sensor recognition command (03:00 back,
                                  04:00 front) is what names the sensor, so it
                                  is where the picture's source is chosen; each
                                  frame takes the newest one and scales it into
                                  the guest's mode with a step accumulator, or
                                  draws the pattern when the phone has sent
                                  nothing (a desktop, a check boot). The front
                                  sensor's module is mounted rotated, so its
                                  picture is turned. A frame size no sensor ever
                                  had is skipped instead of allocated and DMAed.
  contrib/macos-app/…             qemu_ios_camera_frame/flush/sensor/state
                                  (API 2.4): the app's side of the hand-off, with
                                  no device and no guest memory involved.

Nothing here repairs, throttles, retries or waits: the old camera work's
timeouts, parking, fallbacks and extra devices are all gone. The ISP's timing is
the engine's own, untouched, because it is the part that already worked.

